@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About D2DJobs | How We Publish Job Listings";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] = "Learn who runs D2DJobs, how job listings and featured posts are handled, and how to report an issue.";
}

<div class="container py-5 about-page">
    <article class="about-box">
        <h1>About D2DJobs</h1>
        <p class="about-intro">D2DJobs is an independent job-information and career-guidance website for people exploring early-career openings in India. It helps readers find opportunities and compare the facts that matter before they visit an employer's careers site.</p>

        <h2>Who runs D2DJobs</h2>
        <p>D2DJobs is founded and operated by Subash.G. It is not an employer, recruitment agency or government hiring authority. A listing on this website is informational and does not mean that the employer has endorsed D2DJobs, confirmed a candidate's eligibility, or guaranteed an interview or job.</p>
        <p>Questions and corrections can be sent to <a href="mailto:contactsupport21@gmail.com">contactsupport21@gmail.com</a>. When reporting a listing, include its URL and the fact that needs checking. Avoid including personal identity documents or other sensitive information in an email.</p>

        <h2>How job listings are presented</h2>
        <p>We organize job information so readers can review the employer, role, location, qualifications, skills, application route and any published closing date. Where available, a listing links to the employer's recruitment notice or careers page. That original notice is the authoritative source for eligibility and selection rules. Requirements are not inferred when the employer has not stated them.</p>
        <p>Listings can come from employer notices and employer submissions. An employer submission is not automatically published: it must be checked by the site operator and meet the site's publishing requirements. A visible source-check date records when a check was entered in the site; it does not promise that an opening has not changed since then. Employers may close or update a role at any time, so candidates should check the linked source before applying.</p>

        <h2>Featured and paid placement</h2>
        <p>Some listings may receive a clearly labelled featured position. Payment does not guarantee that a listing will be published, change the employer's requirements or bypass review. Advertising and sponsored placement are separate from our job information. Browsing D2DJobs and following a listing's application link are free for job seekers.</p>

        <h2>Career resources</h2>
        <p>Our career guides give general preparation suggestions for applications, interviews and job searches. They are not employer instructions: follow the current vacancy notice when its requirements differ from a guide. Readers can use the linked vacancy and our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> to understand how we present sources and corrections.</p>

        <h2>Report a problem</h2>
        <p>If a job looks expired, its application link fails, or a requirement does not match the employer's current notice, email <a href="mailto:contactsupport21@gmail.com?subject=D2DJobs%20listing%20correction">contactsupport21@gmail.com</a>. We will check the information and update, pause or remove the listing as appropriate.</p>
    </article>
</div>
